From d354ae7742dbeee4e64c6090bf515767275d7653 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BrianMills2718 <69022071+BrianMills2718@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:27:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Unplanned] Sync structured provider attempts get the
 process-side safety ceiling

Emergency: under LLM_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_POLICY=ban a sync structured call had no wall-clock deadline; an OpenRouter call stayed open 15+ minutes and blocked the nightly feedback collector. The async path already wraps attempts in _await_with_safety_ceiling; agent routes keep their own deadline. Tests: 37 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
